    "items": [
      {
        "type": "heading1",
        "verse_numbers": [],
        "lines": [
          "Prayer and Praise for Deliverance from Enemies"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "label",
        "verse_numbers": [],
        "lines": [
          "A Meditation of David, which he sang to the Lord concerning the words of Cush, a Benjamite."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          1
        ],
        "lines": [
          "O Lord my God, in You I put my trust;",
          "Save me from all those who persecute me;",
          "And deliver me,"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          2
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Lest they tear me like a lion,",
          "Rending me in pieces, while there is none to deliver."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          3
        ],
        "lines": [
          "O Lord my God, if I have done this:",
          "If there is iniquity in my hands,"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          4
        ],
        "lines": [
          "If I have repaid evil to him who was at peace with me,",
          "Or have plundered my enemy without cause,"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          5
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Let the enemy pursue me and overtake me;",
          "Yes, let him trample my life to the earth,",
          "And lay my honor in the dust."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "label",
        "verse_numbers": [],
        "lines": [
          "Selah"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          6
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Arise, O Lord, in Your anger;",
          "Lift Yourself up because of the rage of my enemies;",
          "Rise up for me to the judgment You have commanded!"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          7
        ],
        "lines": [
          "So the congregation of the peoples shall surround You;",
          "For their sakes, therefore, return on high."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          8
        ],
        "lines": [
          "The Lord shall judge the peoples;",
          "Judge me, O Lord, according to my righteousness,",
          "And according to my integrity within me."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          9
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Oh, let the wickedness of the wicked come to an end,",
          "But establish the just;",
          "For the righteous God tests the hearts and minds."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          10
        ],
        "lines": [
          "My defense is of God,",
          "Who saves the upright in heart."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          11
        ],
        "lines": [
          "God is a just judge,",
          "And God is angry with the wicked every day."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          12
        ],
        "lines": [
          "If he does not turn back,",
          "He will sharpen His sword;",
          "He bends His bow and makes it ready."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          13
        ],
        "lines": [
          "He also prepares for Himself instruments of death;",
          "He makes His arrows into fiery shafts."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          14
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Behold, the wicked brings forth iniquity;",
          "Yes, he conceives trouble and brings forth falsehood."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          15
        ],
        "lines": [
          "He made a pit and dug it out,",
          "And has fallen into the ditch which he made."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          16
        ],
        "lines": [
          "His trouble shall return upon his own head,",
          "And his violent dealing shall come down on his own crown."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          17
        ],
        "lines": [
          "I will praise the Lord according to His righteousness,",
          "And will sing praise to the name of the Lord Most High."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      }
    ]
  },
